:dimension-stone
    a skos:Collection ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition "Dimension stone is a natural rock material quarried for the purpose of obtaining blocks or slabs that meet specifications as to size (width, length, and thickness) and shape. Dimension stones are used for both exteriors (building cladding, paving) and interiors."@en ;
    skos:historyNote """Barton, WR, 1968, Dimension stone: US Bureau of Mines Information Circular 8391, p. 4.
https://www.usgs.gov/centers/national-minerals-information-center/dimension-stone-statistics-and-information,
https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc170799/,
http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimension_stone""" ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
