:davis-tube-recovery
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :rer-parameters ;
    skos:definition "The Davis tube Recovery (DTR) is a procedure that separates magnetic pulverized iron ore samples into strongly magnetic and weakly or non-magnetic fractions, thus obtaining information on the proportion of an iron ore deposit that is magnetite and the likely grade of concentrate at a given grind size. The separator consists of an inclined tube placed between the pole-tips of an electromagnet; when pulverized material is passed through the tube, the strongly magnetic fraction is held by the magnetic field while the weakly magnetic material is washed down the tube (Davis Tube Wash or DTW)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "Davis Tube Recovery (DTR)"@en ;
    schema:citation
        "https://www.911metallurgist.com/equipment/davis-tube-tester/#"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "https://www.alsglobal.com/en/metallurgy-and-mineral-processing/iron-ore-testwork/iron-ore-magnetite-processing"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

