:alkalis
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Alkali metals are a group of chemical elements that include lithium (Li), sodium (Na), potassium (K), rubidium (Rb), caesium (Cs), and francium (Fr), with sodium and potassium being the most abundant. They are shiny, soft, highly reactive metals at standard temperature and pressure, and tarnish rapidly when exposed to air. All of the discovered alkali metals occur in nature as compounds. They have several and varies applications; amongst others, e.g. sodium chloride is used as table salt or as reducing agent, potassium compounds as fertilizers, lithium in the production of lithium-based batteries and in the processing of silica."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "alkalis"@en ;
    schema:citation "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alkali_hydroxide"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

:alumina-bayer-process
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel
        "aloxide"@en ,
        "aloxite"@en ,
        "alundum"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/alumina> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/alumina> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/alumina> ;
    skos:broader :rer-parameters ;
    skos:definition "The Bayer process is the most commonly used refinement process to remove impurities from the bauxite ore and produce purer alumina. It involves ore digestion in a hot caustic soda solution, the clarification of a sodium aluminate solution and the precipitation of aluminium hydroxide, subsequently calcined to produce alumina. Refinery operation and particularly the processes of gibbsite precipitation and calcination have a profound effect on the properties of the product alumina, and its use in the production of aluminium metal in the Hall-Héroult process."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "alumina extractable by Bayer process"@en ;
    schema:citation
        "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/B978184569654250002X"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/engineering/bayer-process"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

:amazonite
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel
        "amazon jade"@en ,
        "amazon stone"@en ,
