        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/tremolite-actinolite> ;
    skos:broader :asbestos-amphibole ;
    skos:definition "A form of the mineral actinolite that occurs as a fibrous aggregate of crystals (asbestiform) and is recognized as one of the six types of asbestos. Actinolite is a bright green or greyish green monoclinic mineral of the amphibole group and an intermediate member of the actinolite–tremolite series with the chemical formula Ca₂(Mg,Fe)₅Si₈O₂₂(OH)₂. It is commonly found in metamorphic rocks and sheared rocks within fault zones."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "asbestos - actinolite"@en ;
