        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/asbestos-amphibole> ;
    skos:broader :asbestos-amphibole ;
    skos:definition "A fibrous (asbestiform) form of the sodium-rich amphibole mineral riebeckite, with the chemical formula Na₂(Fe²⁺,Mg)₃Fe³⁺₂Si₈O₂₂(OH)₂. Crocidolite, also known as blue asbestos, commonly occurs as soft friable fibres, is one of the six recognized types of asbestos and considered the most hazardous type. In Western Australia crocidolite is found in banded iron-formation in the Hamersley Ranges at Wittenoom."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/crocidolite> ,
