    skos:definition "Banded iron-formation (BIF) is an iron formation that shows marked banding, generally of iron-rich minerals and chert or fine-grained quartz. Typically of Precambrian age, and commonly used for lapidary and decorative purposes."@en ;
    skos:historyNote "Beukes, NJ and Gutzmer, J 2008, Origin and paleoenvironmental significance of major iron formations at the Archean-Paleoproterozoic boundary: Reviews in Economic Geology, v. 15, p. 5–47, doi:10.5382/Rev.15.01." ;
