:borate
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :industrial-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Earth materials that contain economically significant amounts of borate minerals, i.e. minerals characterized by boron oxyanions in their chemical formula (e.g. compounds of BO₃, B₂O₅, B₃O₆, B₂O₄, or [B(O,OH)₄]). Borates can be used for pest control or as fungicide, as flux for borate fusion sample preparation for analysis (e.g. XRF, ICP-MS) and in ceramics and glass making, or as flame retardants."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/borate> ,
