    skos:broadMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/evaporite> ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A variously coloured orthorhombic mineral with the chemical formula KMgCl₃·6H₂O. It forms in marine evaporate deposits where seawater has been concentrated and exposed to prolonged evaporation. Carnallite occurs as a saline residue and is mostly used in fertilizers being an important source of potash."@en ;
