    skos:definition "Cerium is a chemical element with symbol Ce and atomic number 58. It is a soft, silvery, ductile metal that easily oxidizes in air. The minerals monazite and bastnäsite are presently its two most important sources. It is used in the manufacture of pyrophoric alloy."@en ;
