    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "The simplest and most common oxide of the caesium, with the chemical formula Cs₂O. It forms yellow-orange hexagonal crystals. Cesium oxide is used in photocathodes to detect infrared signals in devices such as image intensifiers, vacuum photodiodes, photomultipliers and TV camera tubes."@en ;
