    skos:broader :chalcedony ;
    skos:definition "A variety of chalcedony coloured by iron oxide that is commonly used as a semiprecious gemstone. The colour can vary greatly, ranging from pale orange to an intense almost black. When carnelian grades into brown it is known as sard. Some very dark brown carnelian can be classified as jasper."@en ;
