    skos:broader :chalcedony ;
    skos:definition "An apple-green or pale yellowish-green variety of chalcedony containing finely dispersed nickel minerals and valued as a gem. The darker variety of chrysoprase is referred to as prase; the term prase is also used to describe quartz with chlorite inclusions, and to a certain extent is a colour descriptor, rather than a rigorously defined mineral variety."@en ;
