:chlorite
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :industrial-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A group of platy, mostly monoclinic (also triclinic or orthorhombic) micaceous phyllosilicate minerals. Chlorites have a general chemical formula of A₅₋₆T₄Z₁₈, where A = Al, Fe²⁺, Fe³⁺, Li, Mg, Mn, or Ni, while T = Al, Fe³⁺, Si, or a combination of them, and Z = O and/or OH. Chlorite, both in its mineral form and as a chemical compound, has several uses and applications across various industries and scientific fields, such as disinfectant and oxidizing agent in industrial and agricultural water treatment, bleaching agent in the pulp and paper industry, for drilling mud applications in the oil and gas industry, disinfection and sanitization in medical and food facilities, and to control bacterial and fungal diseases in crops."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/chlorite> ,
