    skos:broadMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/liquid-hydrocarbons> ;
    skos:broader :energy-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Liquid hydrocarbons formed from the condensation of hydrocarbons that are in a gaseous state in a natural underground reservoir. Some gas species within the raw natural gas will condense to a liquid state if the temperature is reduced to below the hydrocarbon dew point temperature at a set pressure. Condensation is caused by a decrease in temperature and/or an increase in pressure."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/condensate> ;
