.

:conglomerate
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :industrial-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A coarse-grained, clastic sedimentary rock, composed of rounded to subangular fragments larger than 2 mm in diameter (granules, pebbles, cobbles, boulders) typically containing fine-grained particles (sand, silt, clay) in the interstices, and commonly cemented by calcium carbonate, iron oxide, silica, or hardened clay. Conglomerate is the consolidated equivalent of gravel both in size range and in the essential roundness and sorting of its constituent particles. The rock or mineral fragments may be of varied composition and range widely in size. Conglomerates may be classified according to nature or composition of fragments, proportion of matrix, degree of size sorting, type of cement, and agent or environment of formation. Conglomerate can be crushed to produce aggregate or as a dimension stone."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "conglomerate"@en ;
    schema:citation "https://glossary.americangeosciences.org/term/conglomerate"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

:copper-specimen
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel "native Cu"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/copper> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/copper> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/copper> ;
    skos:broader :copper ;
    skos:definition "A specimen of the metal copper (Cu) collected, preserved and usually curated as part of a mineral collection. Native copper occurs in oxidized zones of copper deposits and is the only native metal to occur abundantly in large masses. It commonly forms dendritic clusters or mossy aggregates, sheets, or plates filling narrow cracks or fissures, and is prized as a mineral specimen by collectors."@en ;
    skos:historyNote "Compiled by the Geological Survey of Western Australia." ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "copper specimen"@en ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

:cordierite
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel
        "dichroite"@en ,
        "iolite"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A variously coloured orthorhombic mineral with the chemical formula (Mg,Fe²⁺)₂Al₄Si₅O₁₈. It exhibits strong pleochroism, is easily altered by exposure, and is an accessory mineral in granites and a common constituent in metamorphic rocks formed under low pressure. Iolite is the gem variety of cordierite."@en ;
