:cristobalite
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A mineral with the chemical formula SiO₂. It is a high-temperature polymorph of quartz and tridymite and occurs as white octahedrons in the cavities and fine-grained groundmass of acidic volcanic rocks. Cristobalite is stable only above 1470 °C; it has a tetragonal structure (alpha-cristobalite) at low temperatures and a cubic structure (beta-cristobalite) at higher temperatures."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "cristobalite"@en ;
    schema:citation
