    skos:broader :rare-earth-oxides ;
    skos:definition "Dysprosium oxide (Dy₂O₃) is a sesquioxide compound of the rare earth metal dysprosium. It is a pastel yellow–green, slightly hygroscopic powder having specialized uses in ceramics, glass, phosphors, lasers, as a Faraday rotator and dysprosium metal halide lamps."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
