:gallium-oxide
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "An oxide mineral of the element gallium and can refer to two oxide species: gallium(I) oxide, Ga₂O; gallium(III) oxide, Ga₂O₃. Gallium(I) oxide is a brown-black diamagnetic solid which is resistant to further oxidation in dry air. It starts decomposing upon heating at temperatures above 500 °C, and the decomposition rate depends on the atmosphere (vacuum, inert gas, air). Gallium(III) oxide is an inorganic compound and ultra-wide bandgap semiconductor; it is actively studied for applications in power electronics, phosphors, and gas sensing. The compound has several polymorphs, of which the monoclinic β-phase is the most stable."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/galliumoxide> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/galliumoxide> ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "gallium oxide"@en ;
    schema:citation "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallium_oxide"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

