:liquefied-natural-gas
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :petroleum ;
    skos:definition "Natural gas (predominantly methane, CH₄, with some mixture of ethane, C₂H₆) that has been cooled down to liquid form for ease and safety of non-pressurized storage or transport. The primary use of liquefied natural gas (LNG) is to simplify the transport of natural gas from the source to a destination."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "liquefied natural gas (LNG)"@en ;
