:lithium
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel "Li"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A chemical element with symbol Li and atomic number 3. It is a soft, silver-white metal belonging to the alkali metal group of chemical elements. Under standard conditions it is the lightest metal and the least dense solid element. It does not occur freely in nature but occurs mainly as pegmatitic minerals. Lithium and its compounds have several industrial applications, including heat-resistant glass and ceramics, lithium grease lubricants, flux additives for iron, steel and aluminium production, lithium metal batteries and lithium-ion batteries."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/lithium> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/lithium> ,
