        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/gemstone> ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A semitransparent to translucent variety of orthoclase that exhibits a bluish to milky-white pearly or opaline lustre. Flawless moonstones are used as gemstones. The name is sometimes incorrectly applied to peristerite or to opalescent varieties of plagioclase as well as to milky or girasol varieties of chalcedony, scapolite, corundum and other minerals."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
