        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/niobium> ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "An inorganic compound with the chemical formula Nb₂O₅. A colourless, insoluble and fairly unreactive solid, it is the most widespread precursor for other compounds and materials containing niobium. It is predominantly used in alloying, with other specialized applications in capacitors, optical glasses and the production of lithium niobate."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/niobiumpentoxide> ,
