    skos:broader :opal-common ;
    skos:definition "A variety of common opal that is a mixture of chrysotile and opal, or serpentine and opal. It displays chatoyancy (cat's eye effect) from fibrous inclusions within the opal. Siliciophite is yellowish green, yellowish brown and brown in colour and has a resinous or silky lustre."@en ;
