:pozzolana
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel "pozzolan"@en ;
    skos:broader :industrial-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Pozzolans are a broad class of siliceous and aluminous materials which, in themselves, possess little or no cementitious value but which will, in finely divided form and in the presence of water, react chemically with calcium hydroxide [Ca(OH)₂] at ordinary temperatures to form compounds possessing cementitious properties. Naturally occurring pozzolans of volcanic origin are referred to as pozzolana."@en ;
