    skos:definition "A white, colourless, yellow, grey, or red cubic mineral of the halite group with the chemical formula KCl. It is the principal ore mineral of potassium. Sylvite occurs in beds as a saline residue with halite and other evaporites. It has a sharper taste than that of halite."@en ;
