:thallium
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Thallium is a chemical element with the symbol Tl and atomic number 81. It is a grey post-transition metal that is not found free in nature. Commercially, thallium is produced as a byproduct from refining of heavy metal sulfide ores. The majority of thallium is used in the electronics industry, and the remainder is used in the pharmaceutical industry and in glass manufacturing. It is also used in infrared detectors."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/thallium> ,
