:wollastonite
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel "tabular spar"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Wollastonite is a calcium inosilicate mineral (CaSiO₃) that may contain small amounts of iron, magnesium, and manganese substituting for calcium. It is usually white. It forms when impure limestone or dolomite is subjected to high temperature and pressure, which sometimes occurs in the presence of silica-bearing fluids as in skarns or in contact with metamorphic rocks. Wollastonite is used in ceramics, friction products (brakes and clutches), metalmaking, paint filler and plastics."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/wollastonite> ,
