:xenotime
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A group name for tetragonal minerals of the zircon structure type and with the general formula AXO₄, where A = Sc, Y, rare earth elements (REE) or Bi and X = P, As or V. Xenotime occurs as an accessory mineral in granites and pegmatites. Due to uranium and thorium impurities, some xenotime specimens may be weakly to strongly radioactive. Xenotime is used chiefly as a source of yttrium and heavy lanthanide metals (dysprosium, ytterbium, erbium and gadolinium). Occasionally, gemstones are also cut from the finest xenotime crystals."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:narrowMatch
