    skos:broader :rare-earth-oxides ;
    skos:definition "Yttrium oxide, also known as yttria, is Y₂O₃. It is an air-stable, white solid substance. Recovered commercially from monazite sand and from bastnäsite. Widely used: in colour television tubes; to reduce the grain size in chromium, molybdenum, zirconium and titanium; to increase the strength of aluminium and magnesium alloys; as a deoxidizer for vanadium and other nonferrous metals; in nuclear technology for its high neutron transparency."@en ;
