        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/tremolite-actinolite> ;
    skos:broader :asbestos-amphibole ;
    skos:definition "A fibrous (asbestiform) form of the white to dark grey monoclinic amphibole group mineral tremolite with the chemical formula Ca₂Mg₅Si₈O₂₂(OH)₂. Asbestiform tremolite is one of the six recognized types of asbestos. In Western Australia asbestiform tremolite is found in banded iron-formation in the Hamersley Ranges at Wittenoom."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "asbestos - tremolite"@en ;
    schema:citation
