        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/fullers-earth> ;
    skos:definition "An alternate name for palygorskite, i.e. a white, greyish, yellowish, or greyish green chain-structure clay mineral with the chemical formula (Mg,Al)₂Si₄O₁₀(OH)·4H₂O. One of the types of Fuller's earth. This concept is included in the vocabulary because of legacy and production data — its usage is discouraged and palygorskite should be used instead."@en ;
