        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/gemstone> ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A deep-blue to violet-blue monoclinic mineral with the chemical formula Cu₃(CO₃)₂(OH)₂. Azurite is an ore of copper and is a common secondary mineral associated with malachite in the upper (oxidized) zones of copper deposits. Azurite is typically found as tabular to prismatic crystals of a deep \"azure blue\" colour with splendent vitreous faces and is used in pigments, jewellery and as a collector's stone."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/azurite> ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
