:mercury
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel "quicksilver"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A chemical element with the symbol Hg and atomic number 80. A heavy, silvery d-block element, mercury is the only metallic element that is known to be liquid at standard temperature and pressure. Mercury occurs in deposits throughout the world mostly as cinnabar (mercuric sulfide). The red pigment vermilion is obtained by grinding natural cinnabar or synthetic mercuric sulfide. Mercury is used in thermometers, barometers, manometers, sphygmomanometers, float valves, mercury switches, mercury relays, fluorescent lamps and other devices"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/mercury> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/mercury> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/mercury> ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "mercury"@en ;
    schema:citation "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury_(element)"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

:mica
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :industrial-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A group of minerals with the general chemical formula (K,Na,Ca)(Mg,Fe,Li,Al)₂₋₃(OH,F)₂[(Si,Al)₄O₁₀]. The mica group is a large group of sheet silicates that can be parted into flexible or brittle sheets. Micas are prominent rock-forming constituents of igneous and metamorphic rocks, and commonly occur as flakes, scales or shreds. Members of the mica group include muscovite, biotite, lepidolite, phlogopite, zinnwaldite, roscoelite, paragonite and sericite. Micas have a number of applications, e.g. sheet muscovite is used in electric insulators, ground mica in paint and as a dusting agent."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/mica> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/mica> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/mica> ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:narrowMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/sericite> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/sericite> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/sericite> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/sheet-mica> ;
    skos:narrower :lepidolite ;
    skos:prefLabel "mica"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/scrap-mica> ;
    schema:citation
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mica"^^xsd:anyURI ,
