:ornamental-stone
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A mineral or rock having use as an ornamental material including lapis lazuli, onyx, amber, marble, turquoise, petrified wood, jade, malachite and such other specimens. Does not include gemstones. This concept is included in the vocabulary because of unspecified legacy data — its usage is discouraged, as a more specific term (i.e. the actual gemstone) should be used instead."@en ;
    skos:historyNote "Definition compiled from Law Insider's website." ;
