        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/gemstone> ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A chatoyant, translucent to semitranslucent, yellowish brown or brownish yellow gem and ornamental variety of quartz, pseudomorphous after crocidolite, whose fibres (penetrating the quartz) are changed to iron oxide (limonite); silicified crocidolite is stained yellow or brown by iron oxide. Upon heating, the limonite turns to hematite and produces a red to brownish red sheen."@en ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "tiger eye"@en ;
    schema:citation "https://glossary.americangeosciences.org/term/tigerseye"^^xsd:anyURI ;
