    skos:altLabel
        "W(VI) oxide"@en ,
        "W(VI)-oxide"@en ,
        "tungsten oxide"@en ,
        "tungsten(VI) oxide"@en ,
        "tungsten(VI)-oxide"@en ,
        "tungstic anhydride"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Tungsten trioxide is a chemical compound of oxygen and the transition metal tungsten, with the chemical formula WO₃. It is a light yellow crystalline solid. Tungsten trioxide occurs naturally in the form of hydrates, which include the minerals tungstite WO₃·H₂O, meymacite WO₃·2H₂O and hydrotungstite (of the same composition as meymacite, however sometimes written as H₂WO₄). These minerals are rare to very rare secondary tungsten minerals. Tungsten is used in applications such as light bulb filaments, x-ray tubes, welding, superalloys and radiation shielding. It also has use in military sectors (in penetrating projectiles) and in industrial catalysts."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/tungstentrioxide> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/tungstentrioxide> ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:prefLabel "tungsten trioxide"@en ;
    schema:citation
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tungsten_trioxide"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "https://www.mindat.org/min-52513.html"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    schema:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
.

:uranium
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Uranium is a chemical element with symbol U and atomic number 92. It is a silvery grey metal in the actinide series of the periodic table. Uranium is weakly radioactive because all its isotopes are unstable. Many contemporary uses of uranium exploit its unique nuclear properties. Uranium-235 is the only naturally occurring fissile isotope, which makes it widely used in nuclear power plants and military applications."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/uranium> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/uranium> ,
