.

:bismuth
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A chemical element with the symbol Bi and atomic number 83. It is a brittle metal with a silvery-white colour when freshly produced. Elemental bismuth occurs naturally, and its sulfide and oxide forms are important commercial ores. Bismuth compounds account for about half the global production of bismuth. They are used in cosmetics, pigments and pharmaceuticals."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/bismuth> ,
