    skos:definition "A translucent cryptocrystalline variety of chalcedony characterized by variegated colours arranged in alternating stripes or bands, in irregular clouds, or in moss-like forms. Agate is found in virtually all colours, usually of low intensity; it commonly occupies vugs in volcanic rocks and cavities in some other rocks and is prized as an ornamental stone."@en ;
