:chromium
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Chromium is a chemical element with the symbol Cr and atomic number 24. It is a steely-grey, lustrous, hard and brittle metal which takes a high polish, resists tarnishing, and has a high melting point. Chromium is used in chrome plating and alloying for production of corrosion-resistant superalloys, nichrome and stainless steel, as a pigment for glass, glazes and paint, and as an oxidizing agent for tanning leather."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
