:diopside
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A monoclinic mineral of the pyroxene group with the chemical formula CaMgSi₂O₆. Diopside is an important rock-forming mineral in several metamorphic and basic to ultrabasic igneous rocks and is also found in meteorites. Diopside is a part of an important solid solution series of the pyroxene group. It contains little or no aluminium and may contain some iron, and ranges in colour from white to green. Transparent varieties are used in jewellery."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/diopside-enstatite> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/diopside-enstatite> ,
