        "alundum"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A fairly chemically inert, white chemical compound of aluminium and oxygen with the chemical formula Al₂O₃. It is the most commonly occurring of several aluminium oxides, and specifically identified as aluminium(III) oxide. Alumina has a high melting point and is used in the production of aluminium metal, refractories, abrasives and chemicals."@en ;
