:beryl
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:broadMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/gemstone> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/gemstone> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/gemstone> ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A beryllium-bearing aluminium silicate mineral with the chemical formula Be₃Al₂Si₆O₁₈. It usually occurs in green or bluish-green, sometimes yellow or pink, or rarely white, hexagonal prisms in metamorphic rocks and granitic pegmatites and as an accessory mineral in acid igneous rocks. Beryl is an ore of beryllium. Beryl is primarily used as a gemstone."@en ;
