:petroleum
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel
        "crude oil"@en ,
        "oil"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/organic-material> ;
    skos:broader :energy-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A general term for all naturally occurring hydrocarbons, whether gaseous, liquid, or solid, i.e. the complex mixture of mostly hydrocarbons and other organic compounds containing N, O, S, etc., that occur in and on the Earth. As a natural resource, petroleum is most often conceived of in its liquid form, commonly called crude oil, but, as a technical term, petroleum also refers to natural gas and the viscous or solid form known as bitumen, which is found in tar sands.  The term petroleum covers both naturally occurring unprocessed crude oil and petroleum products that consist of refined crude oil, such as combustible fuels, petrochemicals, and lubricants. A fossil fuel, petroleum is formed when large quantities of dead organisms, mostly zooplankton and algae, are buried underneath sedimentary rock and subjected to both prolonged heat and pressure."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/petroleum> ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
    skos:narrower
        :bitumen ,
