:silica
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel
        "silicic oxide"@en ,
        "silicon dioxide"@en ,
        "silicon(IV) oxide"@en ;
    skos:broader :industrial-commodities ;
    skos:definition "The chemically resistant dioxide of silicon with the chemical formula SiO₂. It occurs naturally in several crystalline polymorphs (e.g. the minerals quartz, tridymite, cristobalite, coesite and stishovite); in cryptocrystalline form (chalcedony); in amorphous and hydrated forms (opal); in less pure forms (e.g. sand, diatomite, tripoli, chert, flint); and combined in silicates as an essential constituent of many minerals. It is used in structural materials, microelectronics (as an electrical insulator), and as components in the food and pharmaceutical industries."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
