        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/organic-material> ;
    skos:broader :energy-commodities ;
    skos:definition "Coal is a combustible black or brownish-black sedimentary rock containing more than 50% by weight and more than 70% by volume of carbonaceous material along with variable quantities of other elements, chiefly hydrogen, sulfur, oxygen and nitrogen, derived from fossilized organic remains. Differences in the kinds of plant materials (type), in degree of metamorphism (rank), and in the range of impurity (grade) are characteristic of coal and are used in classification. The hardest form or highest rank is anthracite coal, which can be regarded as metamorphic rock because of exposure to elevated temperature and pressure. Intermediate rank coal is bituminous and low rank coal includes lignite."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch
        <http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/CommodityCodeValue/coal> ,
        <http://resource.geosciml.org/classifier/cgi/commodity-code/coal> ,
        <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/geo-commodities/coal> ;
    skos:historyNote "In GSWA's MINEDEX database 'coal' is also a Target Commodity Group, but is represented in this vocabulary as a parent to all coal commodities." ;
    skos:inScheme cs: ;
