:rare-earth-oxides
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:altLabel "rare-earth oxide"@en ;
    skos:broader :mineral-commodities ;
    skos:definition "A series of inorganic chemical compounds consisting of rare earth elements (REE), from lanthanum (atomic number 57) to lutetium (71), and including yttrium (39) and scandium (21), bonded to an oxygen anion. These elements are not especially rare in the Earth's crust, but concentrations are. The rare earth metals resemble one another very closely in chemical and physical properties, thus making it most difficult to separate them."@en ;
