:mineral-commodities
    a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy cs: ;
    skos:definition "Mineral commodities include: 1) ore minerals, i.e. naturally occurring minerals or mineral groups that contain valuable elements or minerals in sufficient quantities to be economically mined and processed for their desired metal or mineral content; 2) the elements that can be extracted from ore minerals (e.g. niobium, ytterbium); 3) geological materials used for ornamental, lapidary and jewellery purposes (e.g. precious minerals/gemstones, mookaite). The latter category is included under mineral commodities as several commodities can have both industrial and ornamental uses (e.g. garnet)."@en ;
    skos:historyNote "Compiled by the Geological Survey of Western Australia." ;
